meta {
  name: Find Triage Records by Correlation Id
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{CRM_URL}}/rpa_integrationinboundqueues?$select=rpa_integrationinboundqueueid,rpa_name,rpa_errordetails,rpa_processingresult,rpa_processingentity,createdon,modifiedon&$filter=contains(rpa_name,'{{correlationId}}')&$count=true
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  $select: rpa_integrationinboundqueueid,rpa_name,rpa_errordetails,rpa_processingresult,rpa_processingentity,createdon,modifiedon
  $filter: contains(rpa_name,'{{correlationId}}')
  $count: true
}

headers {
  Prefer: odata.include-annotations="OData.Community.Display.V1.FormattedValue"
}

script:post-response {
  const body = res.getBody();
  const count = body['@odata.count'] ?? (body.value ?? []).length;
  console.log(`records for correlationId ${bru.getEnvVar("correlationId")}: ${count}`);
  (body.value ?? []).forEach(r => {
    let details = {};
    try { details = JSON.parse(r.rpa_errordetails ?? '{}'); } catch { details = { raw: r.rpa_errordetails }; }
    console.log(`  ${r.rpa_integrationinboundqueueid}  ${details.failureReason}  created ${r.createdon}  modified ${r.modifiedon}`);
  });
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Every triage record raised for one submission, counted. rpa_name is
  written as "SFD doc upload failure {correlationId}", so a contains match
  on the name finds them all without having to search the Memo field.
  
  This is the idempotency check. Redelivery of a failing message, and replay
  of it from the dead letter queue, must both leave the count at *one* per
  distinct failure reason. The record key is derived — a sha256 of
  correlationId, fileId and failureReason shaped into a GUID — and written
  with If-None-Match: '*', so a repeat write is answered 412 and discarded
  rather than duplicated.
  
  Two things to read carefully:
  
  * *createdon and modifiedon should be identical.* The write is create-only
    and first-write-wins, so a second attempt does not update the record. A
    modifiedon later than createdon means something other than the
    integration touched it.
  
  * *Two records for one correlation id is not necessarily a defect.* The
    key includes the failure reason and the file id, so a submission whose
    files fail for genuinely different reasons raises one record each. Check
    failureReason in the console output before calling it a duplicate.
  
  Set {{correlationId}} by running "List Recent Triage Records" first, or by
  hand if you already have it from the CDP logs.
}
